    "final_text": "I've built the todo CLI with all four commands (`add`, `list`, `complete`, `delete`). The full suite passes: 103 tests, 0 failures, run once through the `full-gate` receipt. ESLint's recommended rules report nothing.\n\n**Files**\n- `index.js`: reads the command line and runs the command. It exits 0 on success; bad input or a broken data file exits 1 with the message on stderr.\n- `lib/todos.js`: the add/complete/delete/list logic and input checks, with no file access.\n- `lib/store.js`: reads and checks `todos.json`, and saves it by writing a temp file and renaming it into place, so a crash mid-write can't leave a half-written file.\n- `package.json`: `npm test` uses Node's built-in test runner, so there's nothing to install.\n- Tests in `test/`: every command is covered for success, missing arguments, invalid IDs, IDs that don't exist, an empty list and a corrupted data file. Some tests also run the real `node index.js`, including 24 `add`s started at once.\n\nTo check that the tests can fail, I broke the code on purpose in 7 ways and confirmed the suite caught each one. The concurrent test missed a shared temp-file name with 8 processes, so I raised it to 24, which caught it 5 out of 5 times.\n\n**Bug found in self-review:** `add \"   \"` against a corrupted `todos.json` reported the corruption instead of the empty text. I fixed it and added a test that fails against the old code.\n\n**Decisions I made where the spec was silent**\n- `todos.json` is a plain JSON array. The next ID is the highest existing ID + 1, so gaps are never refilled. Deleting the todo with the highest ID does let that ID be used again.\n- A missing file counts as an empty list. An empty file, bad JSON, or a malformed todo (bad ID, empty text, non-true/false `completed`, bad timestamp, duplicate IDs) is an error, and the file is left untouched.\n- Unquoted words are joined: `add Buy milk` stores \"Buy milk\". Text is trimmed and can't be blank.\n- IDs must be plain positive whole numbers (`1.5`, `-1`, `0`, `1e3` and `abc` are rejected). `complete` and `delete` take exactly one ID, and `list` takes none.\n- Completing a todo that's already done succeeds with a note and doesn't rewrite the file.\n- I added `help` / `--help` / `-h`. Unknown commands print the usage text and exit 1.\n\n**Deviations**\n- I didn't add a README. The project guidelines say small tools shouldn't get new documents, and `help` shows the usage.\n- Commits are on `feat/cli-todo-app` in conventional-commit format with a Dex co-author line, because the repo's commit hook required both. Nothing is pushed because the repo has no remote. I left `CLAUDE.md` uncommitted since it wasn't mine.\n\n**Possible follow-ups (not built)**\n- **File locking:** two commands running at the same moment can overwrite each other's change. The file never gets corrupted, but one todo can be lost.\n- **Other additions:** completing or deleting several IDs at once, and an \"undo complete\" command.\n- **Multi-line text:** newlines in a todo's text aren't blocked, so they break the one-line-per-todo `list` output.",
